cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExactFrac, please cite the software using the metadata in this file."
title: "ExactFrac"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"

authors:
  - family-names: "Fons"
    given-names: "Cherine"

abstract: >-
  ExactFrac is an exact, certificate-producing implementation of the compact
  positive-integer-multiplicity modified set-pair density problem under the active
  condition f(v) <= d_q(v). The project combines a strongly polynomial exact solver
  architecture with an independent verifier, preregistered oracle expectations,
  adversarial testing, and independently checkable compact witnesses.

repository-code: "https://github.com/Cherine-Fons/ExactFrac"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - combinatorial optimization
  - exact algorithms
  - strongly polynomial algorithms
  - graph algorithms
  - certificate verification
  - compact multiplicities
